(user sign-off on tone before drafting)\n   208\t\n   209\t- At the start of the P6 slice, Architect surfaces the proposed framing to the user before dispatching Codex.\n   210\t- Content should reflect girls' rights to education and to pursue any lawful occupation; women in Nigerian public, professional, and community life; civic equality.\n   211\t- Do not include prescriptive statements about domestic roles, marriage, or reproduction.\n   212\t- Do not introduce content that conflicts with the learner's religious or cultural context without framing it as civic rights, not cultural critique.\n   213\t\n   214\tFamily planning is excluded from `p5-socs-09`. M0 found no supporting public P5 objective, and the official grade document was unavailable. Reconsider only if that official document later confirms the objective and the user explicitly approves reopening the scope.\n   215\t\n   216\t---\n   217\t\n   218\t## 8. Schema contract\n   219\t\n   220\tEvery new module is an object in `content.json.modules[]` with **exactly these keys**, modeled on existing `p2-socs-01`:\n   221\t\n   222\t```json\n   223\t{\n   224\t  \"id\": \"p3-socs-01\",\n   225\t  \"gradeband\": \"p3\",\n   226\t  \"subject\": \"Social Studies\",\n   227\t  \"subjectHa\": \"Nazarin Zamantakewa\",\n   228\t  \"moduleNumber\": 1,\n   229\t  \"titleEn\": \"<English title>\",\n   230\t  \"titleHa\": \"<Hausa title>\",\n   231\t  \"titleAjami\": null,\n   232\t  \"ajami_validated\": false,\n   233\t  \"textExplanationHa\": \"<120–170 words of natural Hausa. Correct hooked letters ɓ ɗ ƙ. Second person, warm, concrete examples from a Northern Nigerian child's world.>\",\n   234\t  \"textExplanationAjami\": null,\n   235\t  \"audioScript\": \"[INTRO] ... [MAIN] ... [PAUSE 1] <question — must exactly match microPauses[0].questionHa> ... [MAIN] ... [PAUSE 2] <question — must exactly match microPauses[1].questionHa> ... [OUTRO] ...\",\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
