rm, Responsibilities and Social Justice; S7 pp. 28–30 | Combined coverage | BEST-EFFORT — NOT VERIFIED AGAINST OFFICIAL NERDC GRADE DOCUMENT | Fundamental-rights categories and UDHR comparison are enrichment. |\n86:| p5-socs-07 | Social Issues — Drug Abuse | S5 public unified SCS P5; S7 Lagos State MoE legacy P5 Social Studies | P5 | Public-source topic family (not official NERDC strand): drug-abuse prevention and coping skills | Public P5 schemes cover effects, early help, prevention, emotion/stress management, communication, peer resistance, goals, and seeking help. | S5 P5 SCS third term, weeks 2–7; S7 pp. 252–253 | Direct coverage | BEST-EFFORT — NOT VERIFIED AGAINST OFFICIAL NERDC GRADE DOCUMENT | Brief intentionally narrows named substances and prohibits operational details. Full Hausa draft requires user sign-off. |\n87:| p5-socs-08 | Social Issues — Conflict and Conflict Resolution | S5 public unified SCS P5; S7 Lagos State MoE legacy P6 Social Studies | P5 | Public-source topic family (not official NERDC strand): conflict resolution, values, and social relationships | Public P5 SCS includes conflict resolution through values; legacy P6 covers group conflict, tolerance, communication, honesty, and cooperation. | S5 P5 SCS first term, Effects of Family Values II; S7 pp. 263–264 | Combined coverage | BEST-EFFORT — NOT VERIFIED AGAINST OFFICIAL NERDC GRADE DOCUMENT | Mediation/dialogue are consistent extensions. Do not use live conflict zones or named militant/sectarian examples. |\n88:| p5-socs-09 | The Nigerian Family — Change and Continuity | S5 public unified SCS P5; S7 Lagos State MoE legacy P5/P6 Social Studies | P5 | Public-source topic family (not official NERDC strand): family values, relationships, and social change | Public sources cover family values/relationships, extended family, and external/social influences on Nigerian family life. | S5 P5 SCS first term, Effects of Family Values; S7 pp. 240–241 and 255–257 | Combined coverage | BEST-EFFORT — NOT VERIFIED AGAINST OFFICIAL NERDC GRADE DOCUMENT | No public source found for family planning as a P5 objective. Exclude family planning unless the official grade document later confirms it. Avoid gender-role stereotypes. |\n89:| p5-socs-10 | Education and Its Importance | S7 Lagos State MoE legacy P6 Civic/Social Studies; S6 public unified SCS P6 | P5 | Public-source topic family (not official NERDC strand): education, empowerment, and citizenship readiness | Public sources cover UBE, education as empowerment, life-long learning, and preparation for greater civic responsibilities. | S7 pp. 34–35 and 261; S6 P6 SCS third term, Preparing for Secondary School Citizenship | Combined coverage | BEST-EFFORT — NOT VERIFIED AGAINST OFFICIAL NERDC GRADE DOCUMENT | Formal/non-formal/informal categories, girl-child education, global literacy, and SDG 4 are enrichment. |\n90:| p5-socs-11 | Nigeria and Africa — ECOWAS and the African Union | S6 public unified SCS P6; S1 context | P5 | Public-source topic family (not official NERDC strand): international relations and regional cooperation | Public P6 SCS scheme groups ECOWAS and the African Union under globalization/international relations and global citizenship. | S6 P6 SCS second term, week 7 | Enrichment | BEST-EFFORT — NOT VERIFIED AGAINST OFFICIAL NERDC GRADE DOCUMENT | Grade-shifted from P6. Verify ECOWAS membership and institutional facts at build time; do not hardcode a stale count. |\n91:| p5-socs-12 | Nigeria and the World — United Nations | S6 public unified SCS P6; S7 Lagos State MoE legacy P6 Social Studies | P5 | Public-source topic family (not official NERDC strand): international organizations and global citizenship | Public sources cover the UN/agencies, international organizations, cooperation, international human rights, and global citizenship. | S6 P6 SCS second term, week 7; S7 p. 264 | Enrichment | BEST-EFFORT — NOT VERIFIED AGAINST OFFICIAL NERDC GRADE DOCUMENT | Grade-shifted. Named UN bodies and Nigeria’s participation need authoritative fact-checking during authoring. |\n92:| p5-socs-13 | Cultural Diversity and National Unity | S5 public unified SCS P5; S7 Lagos State MoE legacy P5/P6 Social Studies/Civic | P5 | Public-source topic family (not official NERDC strand): diversity, social justice, peace, and unity | Public sources cover cultural diversity/unity, fairness, non-discrimination, tolerance, national unity, patriotism, and peaceful coexistence. | S5 P5 SCS first term, Social Justice; S7 pp. 240–241 and 256–258 | Direct coverage | BEST-EFFORT — NOT VERIFIED AGAINST OFFICIAL NERDC GRADE DOCUMENT | NYSC is a brief-selected national-integration example, not exposed in cited objectives. Apply religious/ethnic neutrality controls. |\n93:| p5-socs-14 | Leadership and Good Governance | S5 public unified SCS P5; S7 Lagos State MoE legacy P5 Civic/P6 Civic | P5 | Public-source topic family (not official NERDC strand): leadership, accountability, and good governance | Public P5 scheme covers leader qualities, responsible leadership, transparency, accountability, rule of law, bad governance, and checks on leaders; legacy scheme names ICPC/EFCC functions. | S5 P5 SCS first and second terms; S7 pp. 27 and 35 | Direct coverage | BEST-EFFORT — NOT VERIFIED AGAINST OFFICIAL NERDC GRADE DOCUMENT | Corruption may be defined age-appropriately; institutional roles must be current and nonpartisan. Neutrality review required. |\n94:| p5-socs-15 | Revision and Assessment — P5 Social and Citizenship Studies | S5 public unified SCS P5 | P5 | Public-source topic family (not official NERDC strand): revision and assessment | Public P5 SCS scheme includes review and examination at the end of each term. | S5 P5 SCS first, second, and third terms, weeks 11–12 | Direct coverage | BEST-EFFORT — NOT VERIFIED AGAINST OFFICIAL NERDC GRADE DOCUMENT | AJAMIX review covers its broader proposed sequence. |\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
